2. Modify the program so that it reads 100 characters from stdin and prints them to stdout, but only if they are uppercase letters.
3. Modify the program so that it reads 100 characters from stdin and prints them to stdout, but only if they are lowercase letters.
4. Modify the program so that it reads 100 characters from stdin and prints them to stdout, but only if they are letters.

### Solution

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    // malloc a large buffer and copy in 100 characters from stdin
    char* buf = malloc(1024);
	int i = 0;
	while(i < 1024) {
		buf[i] = getchar();
		i++;
	}

    // print the buffer
    printf("%s", buf);

    // free the buffer
    free(buf);

    return 0;
}
```

### Output

```
