## Explanation

The program reads the file into a buffer, calculates the checksum of the buffer, and saves the number of bytes read and the checksum to a results file.

The checksum is calculated by adding up the ASCII values of each character in the buffer.

The program then checks if the checksum is 0. If it is, the buffer is empty. If it is not, the buffer is not empty.

